// =========================================================
// The brand typeface, for the certificate PDF.
//
// Plus Jakarta Sans — `--font-sans` in globals.css, the face the whole product is set
// in. Certificates were set in Helvetica, which is jsPDF's built-in default and the
// typeface of every unstyled PDF ever generated. Favour, 31 Oct 2026: a certificate
// "has to be unique and branded just for Groundwork."
//
// ── Why the bytes are in a file ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// A PDF embeds its fonts; there is no stylesheet to link and no fallback to a system
// face. jsPDF takes base64 TTF through its virtual file system, so the font has to be
// present at generation time.
//
// ── Why this module is imported lazily ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// These two strings are about 165 KB. `generate-certificate.ts` imports this with
// `await import()`, beside its own `await import('jspdf')`, so neither reaches a
// contractor who never issues a certificate — which is almost all of them.
//
// Latin subset, regular (400) and extra-bold (800), from Google Fonts v12 under the
// SIL Open Font License.
// =========================================================

/** Plus Jakarta Sans Regular (400), base64 TTF. */
export const PJS_REGULAR =
'';

/** Plus Jakarta Sans ExtraBold (800), base64 TTF. */
export const PJS_BOLD =
'';
